From 0bd093e498986155dd46e7ecb61ea13eb2f50826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Nov 2025 17:38:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 685/913] plat-stm32mp1: psci: remove condition on secondary
 CPU for CPU_ON/OFF

This code produce different behavior between STM32MP15 and STM32MP13.

CPU_ON/OFF already reject to do something for CPU#0. We can rely on this
mechanism and remove the property 'enable-method = "psci"' from CPU#0
kernel device-tree node.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 1f7783fbb16f4fef585d0f250b876444fb534d79 plat-stm32mp1: psci: remove condition on secondary CPU for CPU_ON/OFF]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I4d73b87c0c2a9f992485d8f56035370624d0eb62
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/507213
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Tested-by: Jerome BESNARD <jerome.besnard@st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
index 709f833ef..011b934fe 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/plat-stm32mp1/pm/psci.c
@@ -462,9 +462,7 @@ int psci_features(uint32_t psci_fid)
 		return PSCI_RET_SUCCESS;
 	case PSCI_CPU_ON:
 	case PSCI_CPU_OFF:
-		if (stm32mp_supports_second_core())
-			return PSCI_RET_SUCCESS;
-		return PSCI_RET_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+		return PSCI_RET_SUCCESS;
 	case PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF:
 		if (stm32mp_with_pmic())
 			return PSCI_RET_SUCCESS;
-- 
